From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:36:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 185/192] wifi: ath11k: support firmware airtime fairness

Firmware with WMI_TLV_SERVICE_ATF schedules airtime between stations
itself, in proportion to per-station shares the host gives it in parts
per thousand. Enable it at init (resource config flag) and on each
radio, advertise NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AIRTIME_FAIRNESS, and send the
shares of all AP stations of the radio, derived from their airtime
weights (sta_set_airtime_weight), whenever a station associates or
leaves or user space changes a weight.

The firmware schedules a station only within the share of its ATF group,
so group 0, which every station belongs to, first gets the whole radio
(WMI_ATF_SSID_GROUPING_REQUEST_CMDID, fair policy). Without it the
firmware gives each station a share of an empty group and passes no data
to it at all; that was the failure of the first version of this commit.

On the U6 Enterprise's QCN9074 (WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1), a station capped at
100/1000 under strict scheduling falls from 885 to 122 Mbit/s downlink
and recovers once uncapped; at its full fair share it runs at full rate.
mac80211's own airtime scheduler cannot do this here: with the data path
offloaded to NSS, frames never pass mac80211's queues.
